Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-12-2001||12:49 PM||||I have dual opening doors on the back. (It's a large, 3/4 ton chevy van). But the one door won't open.  The door with the outside handle opens fine, and then to get the other door open, there is a small latch right near the ground on the other door, but it doesn't do anything. I tried taking off the inside door panel to see if I could get to it, but that just revealed a wall of sheet metal. Do I actually have to cut a hole there, or is there something I am missing?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-12-2001||10:37 PM||||the outside handle only opens the right hand door, the little lever on bottom of the left door lifts up to open the left door. If it dont work, the center of the inside of the door usually has about a foot square hole in the middle. Just take the upoulstery panel off and reach in, prob just broke the rod off the lever. the connector is only plastic. The panel shouldnt have any screws unless previous owner put some in. just use a wide flat screwdriver and pry the panel loose starting at bottom. If it is all metal with no opening, just cut one with snips or something, panel will cover it up when you put it back on. If I remember right, chevy has bottom catch and a top one both hooked to the little lever.<P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||03-13-2001||12:31 AM||||Thanks man! I'll take a looksy tommorow and let ya know!||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||03-13-2001||04:13 PM||||Man oh man, your foot must be bigger than my foot. It seems the hole is about 5"x5".. Certainly not enough to make use of (even used a mirror). I cut a small extra 1 inch access hole right above the latch, but I can't figure the darn thing out. Don't suppose you'd have a diagram or something? I suppose I might have to unbolt the anchor from the bottom of the door to open it, and then get a good look from the bottom or something. It's kinda snowy right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||03-13-2001||09:28 PM||||LOL, i tried to remember best I could. seemed like we used to put storage shelves in those openings in conversion vans. I try to not take in any body jobs on full size vans, they take up too much space. Once you get in should be pretty cut n dry how to fix it. Latch may just be all rusted, i remember that happening when both doors wearnt used too much.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||03-14-2001||01:48 AM||||Doesn't seem to be rusty. It moves, with little resistance.. something is amiss..||||reg||1
